{"parentUuid":"18302654-ad13-4185-9afc-f8d296cfb76f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01NGBdehgfcDDkicudQqxC1D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Section 2 — Acquisition flow in `entire migrate`\n\nThe lock wraps the entire migration body (including the post-migration generation-metadata repair pass), but **not** flag parsing or help output. Concretely, in `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go`:\n\n```go\nRunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, _ []string) error {\n    if checkpointsFlag == \"\" { return cmd.Help() }\n    if checkpointsFlag != \"v2\" { return fmt.Errorf(...) }\n\n    ctx := cmd.Context()\n    if _, err := paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx); err != nil { /* existing prerequisite check */ }\n\n    // NEW: acquire lock before any state mutation\n    commonDir, err := strategy.GetGitCommonDir(ctx)\n    if err != nil { return NewSilentError(err) }\n    lockPath := filepath.Join(commonDir, \"entire-migrate.lock\")\n    lk, err := lockfile.Acquire(lockPath)\n    if err != nil {\n        if errors.Is(err, lockfile.ErrLocked) {\n            cmd.SilenceUsage = true\n            holderPID := lockfile.ReadHolderPID(lockPath)  // best-effort, returns 0 on read fail\n            fmt.Fprintf(cmd.ErrOrStderr(),\n                \"another `entire migrate` is already running (PID %d, lock at %s); refusing to start a second instance\\n\",\n                holderPID, lockPath)\n            return NewSilentError(errors.New(\"migration already in progress\"))\n        }\n        return NewSilentError(fmt.Errorf(\"acquire migration lock: %w\", err))\n    }\n    defer func() {\n        if relErr := lk.Release(); relErr != nil {\n            logging.Warn(ctx, \"failed to release migration lock\", slog.String(\"error\", relErr.Error()))\n        }\n    }()\n\n    // existing logging init + runMigrateCheckpointsV2(...)\n}\n```\n\n**Lock path lives in the git common dir**, not in `.entire/`. That's the worktree-shared scope we settled on in Question 2. `strategy.GetGitCommonDir` is already cached and cross-platform.\n\n**Acquire is the very first state-touching step.** It runs after flag/prereq validation but before logging init, repository open, or any v1/v2 store calls. That keeps the failure mode obvious: if a second instance starts, it prints exactly one line and exits.\n\n**Release is `defer`-ed.** On normal exit, panic, `cmd.Help()` short-circuit, or any error path, the OS releases the lock. We `defer` rather than rely solely on process death so we can log a release error if the file handle close fails (extremely rare but worth surfacing).\n\n**No `--force-unlock` flag.** Because the OS releases on process death, there's no realistic recovery scenario. If someone genuinely needs to wipe the lock file (say, a busted FS with leaked OS lock state on a network filesystem), they can `rm <lockPath>` manually — we don't need a flag for that.\n\nOK on Section 2?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":103536,"output_tokens":1078,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":103536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CampHomxEYSU17LAWsAVp","type":"assistant","uuid":"45685ff6-ee1d-4e72-bc09-7412e9a2efeb","timestamp":"2026-05-06T18:49:41.889Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/feat/entire-migrate-lock","sessionId":"c1af0c92-59d2-43e5-9cec-afe70cbc425d","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"feat/entire-migrate-lock"}
