{"parentUuid":"d924c4e2-3e70-4e4a-a285-81935a5b9824","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0119mpTDDfRPH5LqTxBtwh5P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Section 3 — Error handling & user-facing messages\n\nThree observable outcomes:\n\n**3a. Acquire succeeds → migration runs as today.** No new output unless we want a debug log on acquire (`logging.Debug(ctx, \"acquired migration lock\", slog.String(\"path\", lockPath))`); user-visible behavior is unchanged.\n\n**3b. Acquire fails with `ErrLocked` → fail-fast, exit non-zero.** Stderr message:\n```\nanother `entire migrate` is already running (PID 12345, lock at /repo/.git/entire-migrate.lock); refusing to start a second instance\n```\nThe PID is best-effort: if the holder hasn't yet written the PID byte (tiny window between `flock()` and `Write()`), or the file is empty/garbage, we print `(PID unknown, ...)`. We use `NewSilentError` so main.go doesn't double-print, and `cmd.SilenceUsage = true` so cobra doesn't dump `--help`.\n\n**3c. Acquire fails with a non-`ErrLocked` error → wrapped and returned.** E.g., \"permission denied,\" \"no such file or directory\" (common dir gone), disk full. These flow through the normal main.go path, no `SilenceUsage`, since they indicate a misconfigured repo, not a contention issue.\n\n**Logging:** acquire and release each emit one `logging.Debug` line with `component=\"migrate-lock\"`, `path=<lockPath>`, and on contention an `INFO`-level line with the holder PID. Per CLAUDE.md, we log operational metadata only — no user content.\n\nOK on Section 3?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":105388,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":544,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":105388,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":""