{"parentUuid":"19fec218-bef3-46da-8408-feba18e4d603","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JT5htSMYB8n2gWpWXwnfn2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Section 4 — Out-of-scope risks flagged for follow-up\n\nPer your instruction to surface (not fix) any regular v2 write paths that could be corrupted by activity during a migration. None block the lock work; flagging here for a separate change.\n\n**4a. `writeMigratedFullGeneration` writes archive refs with blind `SetReference` (`migrate.go:627`).**\nThe migration calls `v2Store.NextGenerationNumber()` to pick the archive slot, then calls `repo.Storer.SetReference(...)` to write `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/<n>` unconditionally. If a concurrent regular condense does `RotateCurrentGenerationIfNeeded` and lands on the same slot in the window between migration's pick and migration's write, migration silently overwrites the regular rotator's archive — lost generation. The lock prevents migration-vs-migration; this is migration-vs-condense. Suggested fix: switch to `CheckAndSetReference` against `plumbing.ZeroHash` (slot must be unallocated when we write) and re-pick on conflict.\n\n**4b. `writeMigratedFinalFullCurrent` is a TOCTOU read-modify-write of `/full/current` (`migrate.go:481+`).**\nIt reads the current ref + tree, merges new entries into the tree map, builds a new commit, and writes the ref. There's no CAS — if a regular writer commits to `/full/current` between the read and the write, either the migration's merged tree drops the regular writer's entries or the regular writer's commit gets parented over by migration's commit. Suggested fix: use `CheckAndSetReference` against the originally-read ref hash; on `ErrReferenceHasChanged`, re-read and retry the merge.\n\n**4c. The migration's `RotateCurrentGenerationIfNeeded` call at `migrate.go:295` is the same function regular condense uses, and that one already has internal CAS guards (lines 530, 583).** This is the safe spot — flagging only because a reader of the diff might wonder why the rotation call doesn't need the same fix. It doesn't.\n\n**4d. `pruneV2CheckpointForForce` (only on `--force`) deletes refs that a regular reader might be in the middle of reading.** Readers using `repo.Reference(refName, true)` will get a clean `ErrReferenceNotFound` rather than corrupted data, so the failure mode is \"user sees a checkpoint disappear from `entire status` mid-read.\" Not a corruption risk, but a UX wart with `--force`. Mentioning for completeness.\n\n**4e. `entire-internal:test-auditor` skill is irrelevant here — just noting that 4a/4b/4c/4d are about *production* coexistence, not test concurrency.** Tests already serialize via `t.TempDir()`.\n\n**Recommendation in the spec:** the lock work proceeds as designed. 4a and 4b should be a follow-up PR titled something like \"fix: use CheckAndSetReference in migration ref writes.\" 4d is a separate UX question.\n\nOK on Section 4?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_read_input_tokens":105388,"output_tokens":1086,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":552,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1086,"cache_read_input_tokens":105388,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":552},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CamxRZGyNReKsTj7zQEBb","type":"assistant","uuid":"65b824cd-a4b6-464c-bd0e-05eb5c689233","timestamp":"2026-05-06T20:36:28.114Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/feat/entire-migrate-lock","sessionId":"c1af0c92-59d2-43e5-9cec-afe70cbc425d","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"feat/entire-migrate-lock"}
