{"parentUuid":"e432237c-c9cc-45d4-adbd-1b39d4a17074","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XJv7mWvjwVekGUxcrQ815w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FEBmrUB6ixGgfb1rJvwXxJ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat <<'EOF' | pbcopy\n# Out-of-scope corruption risks flagged during `entire migrate` lockfile design\n\nRepo: entireio/cli\nWorktree where these were found: .worktrees/feat/entire-migrate-lock\nBranch: feat/entire-migrate-lock\n\n## Context\n\nA separate session is adding a `flock`-based mutual-exclusion lock to\n`entire migrate` (a hidden one-shot command, fail-fast, lock at\n`<git-common-dir>/entire-migrate.lock`). That lock prevents\n**migration-vs-migration** races only.\n\nWhile reviewing the migration flow, the following code paths were flagged\nbecause they can corrupt v2 ref state when a regular v2 write\n(condensation, push, agent-driven rotate) runs concurrently with a\nmigration. The lock does NOT protect these — they are\nmigration-vs-regular-write hazards and need to be fixed independently.\n\nThe user explicitly chose to keep regular v2 writers running during a\nmigration, so these are real production hazards rather than theoretical.\n\n## Risk 4a — `writeMigratedFullGeneration` blind `SetReference`\n\nFile: `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:584-631`\nCritical line: `migrate.go:627`\n\n```go\nif err := repo.Storer.SetReference(plumbing.NewHashReference(refName, commitHash)); err != nil {\n    return fmt.Errorf(\"update migrated generation ref %s: %w\", refName, err)\n}\n```\n\nThe migration loop picks an archive slot via\n`v2Store.NextGenerationNumber()` (`migrate.go:265`) and later writes the\narchive ref with `SetReference` — no CAS, no slot-must-be-unallocated\nguard.\n\nRace window: between migration's `NextGenerationNumber()` call and its\n`SetReference` write. A concurrent regular `RotateCurrentGenerationIfNeeded`\ncan independently pick the same generation number and write to the same\nref. The migration's `SetReference` then silently overwrites the regular\nrotator's archive — **a lost generation, with full transcript content\ngone**.\n\nSuggested fix: use `repo.Storer.CheckAndSetReference(newRef, oldRef)`\nwhere `oldRef` points at `plumbing.ZeroHash` (i.e., the slot must be\nunallocated). On `storage.ErrReferenceHasChanged`, re-pick the next\ngeneration number and retry. The retry must be bounded — fail loudly\nafter, say, 8 attempts to avoid livelock if `NextGenerationNumber` keeps\nreturning a colliding slot for some pathological reason.\n\n## Risk 4b — `writeMigratedFinalFullCurrent` TOCTOU on `/full/current`\n\nFile: `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:481-...` (function body continues past\nline ~580; full body needed for the fix).\n\nThe function:\n1. Reads `/full/current` ref hash + root tree via `v2Store.GetRefState(refName)`.\n2. Flattens the existing tree into an in-memory `map[string]object.TreeEntry`.\n3. Merges the migration's pending entries into that map.\n4. Rebuilds a tree, creates a commit, writes the ref with `SetReference`\n   (no CAS).\n\nIf a regular writer commits to `/full/current` between steps 1 and the\nfinal ref write, one of two things happens:\n\n- The regular writer's tree entries get dropped (migration overwrote\n  them with its merged-from-old-tree map), OR\n- The regular writer's commit becomes orphaned (migration's commit\n  parents over the older state).\n\nSuggested fix: capture the ref hash from `GetRefState` as `expectedRef`,\nthen write with `CheckAndSetReference(newRef, expectedRef)`. On\n`ErrReferenceHasChanged`, re-read the current state and retry the merge\nfrom step 1. Pattern is exactly the same as\n`resetFullCurrentRefIfUnchanged` in\n`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_generation.go:581-591`.\n\n## Risk 4c — Note: rotation at `migrate.go:295` is already safe\n\nThe migration's final\n`v2Store.RotateCurrentGenerationIfNeeded(ctx, batchSize)` call uses the\nsame function as regular condense, and that function already has\ninternal CAS guards\n(`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_generation.go:530, 583`). No fix needed\nhere. Mentioned only because someone reading a diff that fixes 4a/4b\nmight assume this also needs CAS — it doesn't.\n\n## Risk 4d — `pruneV2CheckpointForForce` UX wart (not corruption)\n\nOnly triggered by `entire migrate --checkpoints v2 --force`. Deletes v2\nrefs unconditionally. Concurrent readers using\n`repo.Reference(refName, true)` get a clean `ErrReferenceNotFound`\nrather than torn data, so this is a UX wart (a checkpoint vanishing\nmid-read in `entire status` etc.), not a corruption hazard. Lower\npriority than 4a/4b. Worth mentioning in any documentation around\n`--force` semantics.\n\n## Suggested follow-up PR shape\n\nTitle: `fix: use CheckAndSetReference in migration ref writes`\n\n- Patch 1: `writeMigratedFullGeneration` → CAS-against-ZeroHash + bounded\n  retry on slot collision (Risk 4a).\n- Patch 2: `writeMigratedFinalFullCurrent` → CAS-against-expectedRef +\n  retry-merge loop (Risk 4b).\n- Tests: integration test that spawns one migration and one regular\n  condense concurrently against the same repo and asserts no archive\n  ref is silently overwritten and `/full/current`'s tree contains both\n  contributions.\n\nRisk 4d is a separate UX discussion, not part of this PR.\nEOF\necho \"Copied $(pbpaste | wc -c | tr -d ' ') bytes to clipboard.\"","description":"Copy flagged findings to macOS clipboard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_read_input_tokens":105940,"output_tokens":2279,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1125,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":2279,"cache_read_input_tokens":105940,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1125,"cache_creation":