{"parentUuid":"3f113dec-e2af-41c6-8fc6-fa3b3b35194e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019RgS8ZycXeXD736br6N5rD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Section 5 — Testing strategy\n\nThree layers, each with a clear scope.\n\n**5a. Unit tests for the `lockfile` package** (`cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_test.go`):\n\n- `TestAcquire_FreshFileSucceeds` — acquire on a fresh path returns no error, file exists with mode `0600`, file content equals current PID.\n- `TestAcquire_AlreadyHeldReturnsErrLocked` — first goroutine holds the lock; second `Acquire` on the same path returns `ErrLocked`. Verify the second attempt does NOT clobber the PID byte the first wrote (i.e., the holder's PID is still readable from the file).\n- `TestRelease_PermitsReacquire` — acquire, release, acquire again on the same path succeeds.\n- `TestAcquire_ProcessExitReleases` — spawn a child via `execx.NonInteractive` that acquires and then `os.Exit(0)`s; parent then acquires the same path successfully (exercises kernel auto-release; only meaningful on Unix, gate with build tag).\n- `TestReadHolderPID_*` — empty file returns 0 with no error; garbage content returns 0 with no error; valid PID round-trips.\n- `TestAcquire_PermissionDenied` — point at a path inside an unwritable dir, verify error is wrapped (not `ErrLocked`) and propagates.\n- All tests use `t.TempDir()` and `t.Parallel()` per CLAUDE.md.\n\n**5b. Integration test for `entire migrate` contention** (`cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/migrate_lock_test.go`, `//go:build integration`):\n\n- Set up a tmp repo with a small synthetic v1 checkpoint set via `testutil.InitRepo`.\n- Spawn two `entire migrate --checkpoints v2` processes concurrently using `execx.NonInteractive` (per CLAUDE.md's TTY-detection guidance).\n- Assert exactly one process exits 0 and the other exits non-zero with `another \\`entire migrate\\` is already running` in stderr.\n- Assert v2 state in the repo is consistent with a single successful migration (e.g., expected `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/*` count, no half-written generation).\n- Cleanup: verify the lock file still exists (we don't delete it) but is no longer locked.\n\nTo make the race deterministic without an artificial sleep, the loser process needs the lock to actually be held when it tries to acquire. Cleanest mechanism: a `ENTIRE_MIGRATE_HOLD_LOCK_FOR=<duration>` env var the migrate command honors *only* when set (test-only knob) — after acquiring the lock, sleep for that duration before doing real work. The test sets it on the first process to `2s`, then launches the second, then waits for both. Documented inline as a test-only hook.\n\nI'm flagging the env-var knob explicitly because it's load-bearing for the test design and you may prefer a different mechanism (e.g., a hidden `--test-hold-lock` flag, or refactoring the lock acquisition into something a test harness can call directly). Either works; my preference is the env var because it requires no flag wiring and stays out of `--help`.\n\n**5c. Vogon canary coverage:** the lock work doesn't change agent behavior, so no Vogon test is needed. `mise run test:e2e:canary` should still pass unchanged. Worth running once to confirm.\n\n**Not testing:** Windows behavior (`LockFileEx`) on macOS dev — that's CI's job. The unit-test suite uses build tags so the Unix and Windows shims each get exercised on their native platforms.\n\nOK on Section 5? After this I'll write the design doc to `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-06-entire-migrate-lock-design.md`, commit it, and ask for your spec review before handing off to writing-plans."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":109377,"output_tokens":1325,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":417,"ephe