rom `GetRefState` as\n`expectedRef`; write with `CheckAndSetReference(newRef, expectedRef)`;\non `ErrReferenceHasChanged`, re-read and retry the merge. Pattern\nmatches `resetFullCurrentRefIfUnchanged` in\n`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/v2_generation.go:581-591`.\n\n### 4c. Note: rotation at `migrate.go:295` is already safe\n\nThe migration's final\n`v2Store.RotateCurrentGenerationIfNeeded(ctx, batchSize)` call uses the\nshared rotation function with internal CAS guards — no fix needed.\nDocumented here so a reader of a future 4a/4b fix doesn't conclude this\nneeds the same treatment.\n\n### 4d. `pruneV2CheckpointForForce` UX wart on `--force`\n\n`--force` deletes v2 refs unconditionally. Concurrent readers get\n`ErrReferenceNotFound` rather than torn data — this is a UX wart (a\ncheckpoint vanishing mid-read in `entire status`), not a corruption\nhazard. Lower priority than 4a/4b. Worth mentioning in any\ndocumentation around `--force` semantics.\n\n### Suggested follow-up PR\n\nTitle: `fix: use CheckAndSetReference in migration ref writes`\n\n- Patch 1: `writeMigratedFullGeneration` → CAS-against-ZeroHash with\n  bounded retry (4a).\n- Patch 2: `writeMigratedFinalFullCurrent` → CAS-against-expectedRef\n  with retry-merge loop (4b).\n- Tests: integration test that spawns one migration and one regular\n  condense concurrently and asserts no archive ref is silently\n  overwritten and `/full/current`'s tree contains both contributions.\n\n4d is a separate UX discussion, not part of this PR.\n\n## Testing approach\n\n**Tests are integrated into each implementation step, not deferred.**\nThe writing-plans hand-off must respect this: there is no \"Step N:\nwrite tests.\" Each step that introduces behavior produces the tests\nthat cover it in the same diff. TDD where natural; otherwise tests\nland alongside the code in a single commit.\n\nTest inventory mapped to implementation steps:\n\n### Step: create `lockfile` package\nUnit tests in `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_test.go`, written\nalongside the API:\n\n- `TestAcquire_FreshFileSucceeds` — acquire on a fresh path returns\n  no error; file exists with mode `0600`; content equals current PID.\n- `TestAcquire_AlreadyHeldReturnsErrLocked` — first acquire holds the\n  lock; second acquire returns `ErrLocked`. Verifies the second\n  attempt does NOT clobber the holder's PID byte.\n- `TestRelease_PermitsReacquire` — acquire, release, acquire again on\n  the same path succeeds.\n- `TestAcquire_ProcessExitReleases` (Unix only, `//go:build unix`) —\n  spawn a child via `execx.NonInteractive` that acquires and exits;\n  parent then acquires the same path successfully.\n- `TestReadHolderPID_*` — empty file → 0; garbage → 0; valid PID\n  round-trips.\n- `TestAcquire_PermissionDenied` — unwritable parent dir; verify\n  error is wrapped and is NOT `ErrLocked`.\n\nAll tests use `t.TempDir()` and `t.Parallel()` per CLAUDE.md.\n\n### Step: wire lock into `entire migrate`\nIntegration test in\n`cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/migrate_lock_test.go`\n(`//go:build integration`), in the same commit as the wiring:\n\n- Set up a tmp repo with a small synthetic v1 checkpoint set via\n  `testutil.InitRepo` and existing v1 fixtures.\n- Spawn two `entire migrate --checkpoints v2` processes concurrently\n  via `execx.NonInteractive`.\n- Assert exactly one process exits 0 and the other exits non-zero with\n  `another \\`entire migrate\\` is already running` in stderr.\n- Assert v2 state is consistent with a single successful migration:\n  expected `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/full/*` count, no\n  half-written generation.\n- Verify the lock file still exists post-migration (we don't delete it)\n  but is no longer locked (third invocation succeeds).\n\nTo make the race deterministic without a sleep, the migrate command\nhonors a test-only env var\n`ENTIRE_MIGRATE_HOLD_LOCK_FOR=<duration>` — when set, it sleeps for\nthat duration immediately after acquiring the lock. The test sets it\nto `2s` on the first process and launches the second within that\nwindow. The hook lives in `migrate.go` behind an `interactive.UnderTest()`-style\nguard so production binaries do not respect it. (Alternative: a hidden\n`--test-hold-lock` flag. Env var preferred because it requires no\nflag wiring and stays out of `--help`.)\n\n### Sanity check at end\n`mise run test:e2e:canary` (Vogon) is run as a regression check. The\nlock work does not change agent behavior, so no new canary tests are\nexpected; this is the same end-of-change check every diff gets.\n\n### Not tested locally\nWindows-side `LockFileEx` behavior is exercised in CI on its native\nplatform. Build tags ensure each shim is compiled and tested on the\nplatform that matters.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **PID file + `kill -0` content check.** Simpler portably, but stale\n  locks (kill -9, container teardown, NFS) are a real recovery\n  problem. OS-level lock with auto-release on process death is\n  strictly better.\n- **Block-and-serialize on contention** (with or without timeout).\n  Considered and rejected. `entire migrate` is one-shot and\n  user-initiated; a clear \"another migration is in progress\" message\n  beats hanging in a script. Block-with-timeout has the same\n  implementation cost as fail-fast plus extra plumbing for no clear\n  win.\n- **Per-worktree lock at `.entire/migrate.lock`.** Wrong scope —\n  migration mutates shared `.git/` refs, so two worktrees would still\n  race. Rejected.\n- **Machine-global lock in `~/.entire/`.** Wrong scope in the other\n  direction — would block migrating two unrelated repos\n  simultaneously. Rejected.\n- **Migration takes exclusive lock; all v2 writers take shared\n  lock.** Solves migration-vs-regular hazards too, but would require\n  threading `LOCK_SH` acquisitions through every v2 write path —\n  disproportionate for a one-shot tool. The smaller-scoped follow-up\n  PR for risks 4a/4b uses CAS instead, which is local and sufficient.\n- **`gofrs/flock` external dep.** Unnecessary; `golang.org/x/sys` is\n  already a transitive dep and provides the primitives directly.\n\n## Implementation considerations\n\n- The `tryLockExclusive` shim is the only OS-conditional code; the\n  rest of the package (file open, PID write, error wrapping) is\n  cross-platform. This keeps the build-tag surface minimal.\n- The `ENTIRE_MIGRATE_HOLD_LOCK_FOR` env var is a deliberate test-only\n  hook. Document it inline at the read site as such, gate it behind a\n  helper that is only meaningful under test, and do not surface it in\n  `--help` or any user-facing docs.\n- No new top-level dependencies. `golang.org/x/sys` is already\n  pulled in transitively.\n- File mode `0600` because the lock file lives inside `.git/` and only\n  the user should be able to inspect or stat it.\n- `O_CLOEXEC` on the open call so that any subprocess we might spawn\n  during the migration does not inherit an open file descriptor for\n  the lock — keeping the lock lifetime tied strictly to the migrate\n  process.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1026,"cache_read_input_tokens":112001,"output_tokens":6627,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1026,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":6627,"cache_read_input_tokens":112001,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1026},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CamzQ1j89vCiMdPpsVsD2","type":"assistant","uuid":"146d63c6-973c-477f-8ee7-b2ec57be4569","timestamp":"2026-05-06T21:03:49.053Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/feat/entire-migrate-lock","sessionId":"c1af0c92-59d2-43e5-9cec-afe70cbc425d","version":"2.1.119","gitBra