{"parentUuid":"8a3361d4-f1ec-41dd-93ae-b2ddc8b5470d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FfN82JCPVB7Gp66BEDiv2y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011rXJpDxBXpsD7aHxRXQt39","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/feat/entire-migrate-lock/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-06-entire-migrate-lock.md","content":"# `entire migrate` mutual-exclusion lock — implementation plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Prevent two `entire migrate` invocations from concurrently mutating v2 ref state in the same git repository by adding a fail-fast OS-level file lock.\n\n**Architecture:** A new `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile` package wraps `flock` (Unix) / `LockFileEx` (Windows) behind a small cross-platform API (`Acquire` / `Release` / `ReadHolderPID`). `entire migrate` acquires the lock at `<git-common-dir>/entire-migrate.lock` immediately after prerequisite validation; on contention it prints the holder PID and exits non-zero. The OS releases the lock on process death, eliminating the stale-lock recovery problem.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26.x, `golang.org/x/sys/unix`, `golang.org/x/sys/windows` (already transitive deps), cobra, testify.\n\n**Constraints carried from the spec:**\n- Tests live in the same commit as the code that introduces the behavior. There is no dedicated \"write tests\" task.\n- Each task is one approval unit per the user's \"Plan First\" workflow. The user approves Task 1's diff before we start Task 2.\n- `mise run check` (lint/build/test) runs at the end of each task as part of standard verification, not as its own task.\n- Out-of-scope risks 4a–4d in the spec are NOT part of this plan and are tracked separately.\n\n**Plan file is git-ignored per CLAUDE.md (`docs/superpowers/`). Do not commit it.**\n\n---\n\n## File Structure\n\n**Created files:**\n\n| Path | Responsibility |\n| --- | --- |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile.go` | Public API: `Lock`, `ErrLocked`, `Acquire`, `Release`, `ReadHolderPID`, `writePID`. Cross-platform; calls `tryLockExclusive` / `unlock`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_unix.go` | `//go:build unix` — implements `tryLockExclusive` and `unlock` via `unix.Flock`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_windows.go` | `//go:build windows` — implements `tryLockExclusive` and `unlock` via `windows.LockFileEx` / `UnlockFileEx`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_test.go` | Cross-platform unit tests for `Acquire`, `Release`, `ReadHolderPID`. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_unix_test.go` | `//go:build unix` — subprocess test verifying kernel auto-release on process death. |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/migrate_lock_test.go` | `//go:build integration` — concurrent `entire migrate` contention test. |\n\n**Modified files:**\n\n| Path | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go` (`RunE` body, currently lines 42–66) | Acquire lock immediately after `paths.WorktreeRoot` check; honor test-only `ENTIRE_MIGRATE_HOLD_LOCK_FOR` env var; defer release. |\n\n---\n\n## Task 1: Create `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile` package\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_unix.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_windows.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_unix_test.go`\n\nThis task delivers a self-contained, tested lockfile package. No callers exist yet — that's Task 2.\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write the test file `lockfile_test.go`**\n\nCreate `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_test.go`:\n\n```go\npackage lockfile_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"bytes\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/lockfile\"\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert\"\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n)\n\nfunc TestAcquire_FreshFileSucceeds(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tpath := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"test.lock\")\n\n\tlk, err := lockfile.Acquire(path)\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\trequire.NotNil(t, lk)\n\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = lk.Release() })\n\n\tinfo, err := os.Stat(path)\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\tassert.Equal(t, os.FileMode(0o600), info.Mode().Perm(), \"lock file must be 0600\")\n\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\tpid, parseErr := strconv.Atoi(string(bytes.TrimSpace(data)))\n\trequire.NoError(t, parseErr)\n\tassert.Equal(t, os.Getpid(), pid)\n}\n\nfunc TestAcquire_AlreadyHeldReturnsErrLocked(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tpath := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"test.lock\")\n\n\tlk1, err := lockfile.Acquire(path)\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = lk1.Release() })\n\n\tlk2, err := lockfile.Acquire(path)\n\tassert.Nil(t, lk2)\n\trequire.Error(t, err)\n\tassert.True(t, errors.Is(err, lockfile.ErrLocked), \"expected ErrLocked, got %v\", err)\n\n\t// First holder's PID is still present — second attempt must NOT clobber it.\n\tassert.Equal(t, os.Getpid(), lockfile.ReadHolderPID(path))\n}\n\nfunc TestRelease_PermitsReacquire(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tpath := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"test.lock\")\n\n\tlk1, err := lockfile.Acquire(path)\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\trequire.NoError(t, lk1.Release())\n\n\tlk2, err := lockfile.Acquire(path)\n\trequire.NoError(t, err)\n\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = lk2.Release() })\n}\n\nfunc TestReadHolderPID_EmptyFile(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tpath := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"test.lock\")\n\trequire.NoError(t, os.WriteFile(path, []byte{}, 0o600))\n\tassert.Equal(t, 0, lockfile.ReadHolderPID(path))\n}\n\nfunc TestReadHolderPID_GarbageContent(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tpath := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"test.lock\")\n\trequire.NoError(t, os.WriteFile(path, []byte(\"not a number\"), 0o600))\n\tassert.Equal(t, 0, lockfile.ReadHolderPID(path))\n}\n\nfunc TestReadHolderPID_MissingFile(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tpath := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"missing.lock\")\n\tassert.Equal(t, 0, lockfile.ReadHolderPID(path))\n}\n\nfunc TestAcquire_PermissionDenied(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\tif os.Getuid() == 0 {\n\t\tt.Skip(\"root bypasses permission checks\")\n\t}\n\tdir := t.TempDir()\n\trequire.NoError(t, os.Chmod(dir, 0o500))\n\tt.Cleanup(func() { _ = os.Chmod(dir, 0o700) })\n\n\tpath := filepath.Join(dir, \"test.lock\")\n\tlk, err := lockfile.Acquire(path)\n\tassert.Nil(t, lk)\n\trequire.Error(t, err)\n\tassert.False(t, errors.Is(err, lockfile.ErrLocked), \"permission errors must NOT be ErrLocked\")\n}\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write the Unix-only subprocess test `lockfile_unix_test.go`**\n\nCreate `cmd/entire/cli/lockfile/lockfile_unix_test.go`:\n\n```go\n//go:build unix\n\npackage lockfile_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/exec\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/lockfile\"\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/assert\"\n\t\"github.com/stretchr/testify/require\"\n)\n\n// TestAcquire_ProcessExitReleases verifies kernel auto-release on\n// process death. The child re-execs this binary with role=\"child\", which\n// acquires the lock and exits — the kernel releases the flock when the\n// FD closes. The parent then re-acquires the same path.\nfunc TestAcquire_ProcessExitReleases(t *testing.T) {\n\tt.Parallel()\n\n\tif os.Getenv(\"LOCKFILE_TEST_CHILD\") == \"1\" {\n\t\t// Child role: acquire, print marker, exit.\n\t\tpath := os.Getenv(\"LOCKFILE_TEST_PATH\")\n\t\t_, err := lockfile.Acquire(path)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tos.Stderr.WriteString(\"CHILD_FAIL: \" + err.Error())\n\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t}\n\t\tos.Stderr.WriteString(\"CHILD_ACQUIRED\")\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\t}\n\n\tpath := filepath.Join(t.TempDir(), \"test.lock\")\n\n\tctx, c